.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-DELETE-TOPIC-TAG 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic-tag \- delete a tag from a topic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens delete-topic-tag
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a tag from a topic identified by its Euclid resource name (ERN).
.PP
.B Not yet functional in this release:
this command currently sends its request to the
.I eqs
service instead of
.IR ens ,
so it cannot succeed against a topic regardless of arguments. Both this
routing issue and the lack of a server-side handler (see
.BR euclid-cli-ens-add-topic-tag (1))
need to be fixed before this action works.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the topic to remove the tag from. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key of the tag to delete. Required.
.PP
The topic may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tag was deleted. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or
(currently, always) the request cannot be routed to the topic.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens delete-topic-tag \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:topic:order-events \e
    --key team
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-add-topic-tag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-topic-tag (1)
